            "With string and bamboo"
          ],
          "a": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r20261106-a02",
      "title": "Libraries That Lend More Than Books",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "When you think of a library, you probably imagine shelves of books. But in many cities, libraries now lend much more than that. You can borrow a drill, a sewing machine, a guitar, or even a packet of seeds for your garden.",
        "The idea started from a simple question: why should every family buy things they only use once or twice a year? A drill, for example, is used for about fifteen minutes in its whole life. Sharing tools saves money and reduces waste. Members pay a small yearly fee, or sometimes nothing at all.",
        "These new libraries also teach skills. Volunteers show people how to use the tools safely. \"We are not just lending things,\" says one librarian. \"We are building a community that shares.\""
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "lend": "meminjamkan",
        "borrow": "meminjam",
        "drill": "bor",
        "sewing machine": "mesin jahit",
        "seeds": "biji/benih",
        "waste": "limbah",
        "fee": "biaya",
        "safely": "dengan aman"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What can people borrow from these libraries besides books?",
          "opts": [
            "Cars and motorbikes",
            "Food and drinks",
            "Tools, instruments, and seeds"
          ],
          "a": 2
        },
        {
          "q": "According to the text, how long is a drill usually used in its whole life?",
          "opts": [
            "About fifteen hours",
            "About fifteen minutes",
            "About fifteen days"
          ],
          "a": 1
        },
        {
          "q": "What is the main idea of these libraries?",
          "opts": [
            "Making money from members",
            "Replacing all book libraries",
            "Building a community that shares"
          ],
          "a": 2
        }
      ]
